But if you don't have 300 HP and AC -30 you've intentionally crippled
yourself; they are readily available and if the objective is to ascend you
should have them.

Equally well, however, the answer to mistakes is not an AoLS; it's not to
make mistakes.

I think the argument for ESP is more that it makes speedy travel more easy
during the final run, and slow travel directly drains resources.

The real problem here, however, is that for an experienced player the
post-Castle-wand game is trivial - "solved", as Derek has it. A good
player should *never* lose a character after the Castle wand. Given that,
it's easy to argue that any given piece of the AK that makes a small
contribution can be omitted. I think people differ here because of the way
in which they are not as good as they could be. If you are prone to make
mistakes, you want an AoLS. If you are prone to not maximising HP and AC,
you want ESP. If (like me) you worry about running out of resources, you
want ESP and other speedy travel items.
